====Verb====
{{en-verb}} {{term-label|en|British spelling}}

# {{lb|en|transitive}}
## To [[detect]] (a [[flavor#Noun|flavour]] or [[taste#Noun|taste]], or [[food]] or [[drink#Noun|drink]]); to [[taste#Verb|taste]]; specifically, to [[enjoy]] or [[linger]] on (a flavour or taste, or food and drink); to [[relish#Verb|relish]].
##: {{ux|en|He closed his eyes so he could really '''savour''' his dessert.}}
## To [[give#Verb|give]] (food or drink) flavour; to [[flavor#Verb|flavour]], to [[season#Verb|season]].
##* '''1974''', W. R. Barron, ''{{w|Sir Gawain and the Green Knight}}'' (modern translation)
##*: {{...}} divers sorts of fish; some baked in bread, some broiled on the coals, some seethed, some in gravy '''savoured''' with spices, and all with condiments so cunning that it caused him delight.
## {{lb|en|archaic}} To detect (an [[aroma]] or [[smell#Noun|smell]], especially an [[appealing#Adjective|appealing]] one); to [[smell#Verb|smell]].
## {{lb|en|figurative}}
### To enjoy (something) [[deeply]] or in a lingering [[manner#Noun|manner]]; to [[appreciate]], to [[delight in]], to relish.
###* {{quote-journal|en|date=2020 August 26|author=Andrew Mourant|title=Reinforced against future flooding|journal=Rail|page=58|passage=A journey along the Conwy Valley line is one to '''savour''' for aficionados of scenic railways.}}
### {{lb|en|chiefly in the negative}} To [[find#Verb|find]] (something) appealing; to appreciate, to [[like#Verb|like]].
###: {{synonyms|en|care for}}
### {{lb|en|archaic}} To [[possess]] (a [[particular#Adjective|particular]], often [[negative#Adjective|negative]], [[quality#Noun|quality]]), especially a [[small#Adjective|small]] [[amount#Noun|amount]] of it; to be [[redolent]] or [[suggestive]] of (something).
### {{lb|en|obsolete}} To be appealing to (a person, the [[sense#Noun|senses]], etc.).
### {{lb|en|obsolete}} To [[experience#Verb|experience]], [[perceive]], or [[understand]] (something).
### {{lb|en|obsolete}} To give (something) a particular quality; to [[imbue]] with.
### {{lb|en|obsolete|rare}} To give (something) an aroma or smell.
### {{lb|en|obsolete|rare}} ''Followed by'' '''[[out#Preposition|out]]''': to detect or find (something).
### {{lb|en|obsolete|uncertain}} To have a [[suspicion]] of (something).
# {{lb|en|intransitive}}
## {{lb|en|archaic}} Of a [[thing]]: to [[give off]] a ([[specified#Adjective|specified]]) aroma or smell.
## {{lb|en|archaic|or|obsolete}} Of food or drink: to have a specified (especially appealing) flavour or taste.
## {{lb|en|figurative}}
### To possess a particular (often negative) quality, especially a small amount of it; to be redolent or suggestive of.
###* {{RQ:Shakespeare Twelfth Night|V|i|passage=This '''savours''' not much of distraction.}}
###* {{RQ:Spectator|issue=262|date=31 December 1711|passage=I have rejected everything that '''savours''' of party.}}
###* {{quote-text|en|year=1750|author=w:Joseph Bellamy|title=True Religion Delineated|passage=Begone, thou impudent wretch, to hell, thy proper place: thou art a despiser of my glorious majesty, and your frame of spirit '''savours''' of blasphemy.}}
### {{lb|en|archaic}} ''Chiefly followed by a [[descriptive#Adjective|descriptive]] [[word#Noun|word]] like'' '''[[ill#Adjective|ill]]''' ''or'' '''[[well#Adjective|well]]''': to have a [[specified#Adjective|specified]] quality.
## {{lb|en|obsolete}}
### To give off a [[foul#Adjective|foul]] smell; to [[stink#Verb|stink]].
### {{lb|en|figurative}} ''Chiefly followed by'' '''[[to#Preposition|to]]''''','' '''[[unto#Preposition|unto]]''''','' '''[[with#Preposition|with]]''''', etc.'': to be appealing.

